>>
Rule 1 (input must have a tensor dtype, not str or np.dtype)
{v_1 : tensor} |= 0 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10
>>
Rule 2 (input cannot have string-like dtypes)
{v_1 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_1) ≠ 11 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≠ 12
>>
Rule 3 (all dimension sizes are non-negative)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 4 (supports real and complex numeric dtypes)
{v_1 : tensor} |= (dtype_(v_1) ≤ 8) ∨ (dtype_(v_1) = 9) ∨ (dtype_(v_1) = 10)
>>
Rule 5 (scalar tensors are valid inputs)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = 0 ∨ ndim(v_1) ≥ 1
